title: Outer Rim Affairs
subtitle: Relief, piracy, slavery and representation for the Rim.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_rim.svg
view-if: rimaffairs_timer <= 0 and chair_rimaffairs = "rc" and cardok_rimaffairs
on-arrival: {! Q.turn_actions += 1; Q.rimaffairs_timer = 3; Q.last_card_timer = 'rimaffairs'; SW.porkPick(Q, 'rimaffairs'); !}
new-page: true
on-display: {! SW.cardStuck(Q, this); !}

= Outer Rim Affairs Committee

The Caucus chairs the Outer Rim Affairs Committee. Hardship on the Rim is [+ rim_hardship : level +].

- @relief_act: Put the Rim Relief Act to the Senate.
- @relief: Launch a Rim relief programme.
- @piracy: Fund anti-piracy patrols.
- @slavery_report: Commission a Senate report on slavery.
- @abolition: Abolish slavery in Hutt space.
- @enforce: Enforce abolition.
- @enfranchise: Pass the Rim Enfranchisement Act.
- @assembly: Found a Rim Assembly.
- @sentience: Proclaim the Rights of Sentience.
- @hearings: Hold committee hearings on the Rim.
- @patronage_1: Route relief contracts through friendly governors.
- @patronage_2: Build hyperspace beacons in friendly sectors.
- @patronage_3: Grant colonisation charters to friends.
- @patronage_4: Recognise friendly claimants in disputed Rim systems.
- @patronage_5: Sell Rim mining charters to friendly Core firms.
- @patronage_6: Pay friendly Mid Rim worlds to resettle Rim refugees.
- @easy_discard
- @set_aside

@relief
view-if: rim_hardship > 15
subtitle: −2 treasury. A lasting reduction in Rim hardship.
choose-if: treasury >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 2; rim_relief += 1; rim_hardship -= 4; outer_sep -= 2; rim_relation += 3

The Rim Relief Programme funds clinics, shipyards and grain ships for a hundred worlds.

@piracy
view-if: rim_hardship > 20 and not war
subtitle: −1 treasury. Less hardship; the Security Bloc approves.
choose-if: treasury >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The treasury cannot afford it.
on-arrival: treasury -= 1; rim_hardship -= 2; sec_relation += 3; judicial_forces += 0.2

Judicial patrol frigates begin escorting convoys through the Rim's worst lanes.

@abolition
view-if: not slavery_abolished and slavery_report
subtitle: −1 political capital. A historic act. The Hutts will retaliate.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.rimaffairs_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.3, rim: 0.7, sec: 0.45, ind: 0.45, pal: 0.4, cis: 0.2}, true);
st.rim += Q.slavery_campaign * 0.05; st.mod += Q.slavery_campaign * 0.05;
Q.ab_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['rim', 'slavery']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Abolition of Slavery Act', Q.ab_vote);
if (Q.ab_vote >= 50) {
    Q.slavery_abolished = 1; Q.rim_hardship += 2; Q.rim_relation += 6; Q.faith += 2; Q.anakin_fall -= 1;
    Q.outer_rc += 1.5; Q.midrim_rc += 1.5; Q.colonies_rc += 0.5; SW.computeSupport(Q);
    this.achieve('abolition');
}
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if slavery_abolished : Slavery is outlawed throughout the Republic and its client territories, Hutt space included. The cartels respond with raids and blockades, but slave markets from Tatooine to Nar Shaddaa begin to empty. ?][? if not slavery_abolished : The Hutts' friends in the Senate quietly kill the bill. ?]

@enfranchise
view-if: not rim_enfranchised and rim_relief_act
subtitle: −1 political capital. Full representation for the Rim: a lasting cure for separatism, if it passes.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rc_in_govt
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital and a seat in government.
on-arrival: {!
Q.rimaffairs_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.35, guild: 0.25, rim: 0.95, sec: 0.2, ind: 0.6, pal: 0.35, cis: 0.7}, true);
Q.en_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['rim', 'representation']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Rim Enfranchisement Act', Q.en_vote);
if (Q.en_vote >= 50) { Q.rim_enfranchised = 1; Q.outer_sep -= 10; Q.midrim_sep -= 6; Q.rim_relation += 10; Q.mod_relation -= 5; Q.outer_rc += 3; this.achieve('enfranchised'); }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if rim_enfranchised : Outer Rim sectors gain the delegations their populations deserve, and seats on every major committee. For the first time in centuries, the Rim has a real voice in the Republic. ?][? if not rim_enfranchised : The Core will not share power. The Rim takes note. ?]

@hearings
subtitle: Free. The Rim is heard; builds the case for abolition.
on-arrival: rim_relation += 3; outer_sep -= 1; slavery_campaign += 0.3

Rim witnesses testify before the committee. Their stories make the news.

@relief_act
view-if: not rim_relief_act
subtitle: −1 political capital. A standing commitment to the Rim, if the Senate agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.rimaffairs_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.5, guild: 0.35, rim: 0.9, sec: 0.35, ind: 0.6, pal: 0.4, cis: 0.7}, true);
Q.ra_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, 'rim');
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Rim Relief Act', Q.ra_vote);
if (Q.ra_vote >= 50) { Q.rim_relief_act = 1; Q.rim_relief += 1; Q.rim_hardship -= 3; Q.rim_relation += 4; Q.outer_sep -= 2; Q.midrim_sep -= 1; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if rim_relief_act : The Rim Relief Act passes. Relief for the Rim is no longer a favour the Core grants in a good year: it is the law, with a budget line of its own. ?][? if not rim_relief_act : The Act fails. Relief stays at the mercy of each year's budget. ?]

@assembly
view-if: rim_enfranchised and not rim_assembly
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Rim governs its own affairs within the Republic, if the Senate agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and rim_relation >= 55
unavailable-subtitle: [? if rim_relation < 55 : The Rim does not trust us enough yet. ?][? if rim_relation >= 55 : Needs 1 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.rimaffairs_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.3, guild: 0.25, rim: 0.95, sec: 0.2, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.25, cis: 0.8}, true);
Q.as_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['rim', 'representation']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Rim Assembly Act', Q.as_vote);
if (Q.as_vote >= 50) {
    Q.rim_assembly = 1; Q.outer_sep -= 15; Q.midrim_sep -= 15; Q.rim_relation += 8; Q.rimward_dissent -= 8;
    Q.sep_momentum = (Q.sep_momentum || 0) * 0.5; Q.mod_relation -= 4; this.achieve('assembly');
}
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if rim_assembly : The Rim Assembly meets for the first time on Ord Mantell: a parliament for the Mid and Outer Rim, with its own budget and the right to run its own affairs within the Republic. The Separatists' envoys find the Rim's worlds suddenly less interested in leaving. ?][? if not rim_assembly : The Core's delegations will not share sovereignty. The Rim takes note, and Raxus takes heart. ?]

@slavery_report
view-if: not slavery_report
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Senate's own record of the slave trade.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {! Q.capital -= 1; Q.slavery_report = 1; Q.slavery_campaign += 0.5; Q.anakin_fall -= 1; Q.outer_rc += 1.5; Q.midrim_rc += 1.5; Q.colonies_rc += 0.5; SW.computeSupport(Q); Q.rimaffairs_timer = 1; !}

The committee's report runs to four thousand pages: the slave markets of Tatooine and Nar Shaddaa, the Zygerrian slavers, the shipping lines that carry their cargo and the senators who look away. It is read into the record, page by page, and the HoloNet broadcasts every word. [? if anakin_found : Somewhere in the Temple, a young Jedi reads it all. ?]

@enforce
view-if: slavery_abolished and not slavery_enforced
subtitle: −1 political capital. Send the Judicial Forces into the slave markets.
choose-if: capital >= 1 and syndicates_broken
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not syndicates_broken : The slave markets are protected by the syndicates. ?][? if syndicates_broken : Needs 1 political capital. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.rimaffairs_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1; Q.slavery_enforced = 1; Q.anakin_fall -= 1; Q.rim_relation += 5; Q.faith += 1;
Q.outer_rc += 2; Q.midrim_rc += 2; Q.colonies_rc += 0.5;
if (!Q.shmi_freed && !Q.shmi_dead) { Q.shmi_freed = 1; Q.shmi_freed_now = 1; }
SW.computeSupport(Q);
!}

Judicial frigates land on Tatooine, Nar Shaddaa and Zygerria with abolition orders and the force to back them. Chains are cut in the open, on the HoloNet, in markets that have traded people for a thousand years.

@sentience
view-if: not sentience_rights
subtitle: −1 political capital. Equal rights for every sentient being, if the Senate agrees.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 1 political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.rimaffairs_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.55, guild: 0.45, rim: 0.85, sec: 0.25, ind: 0.65, pal: 0.2, cis: 0.6}, true);
Q.sr_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['rim', 'xenos']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Declaration of the Rights of Sentience', Q.sr_vote);
if (Q.sr_vote >= 50) { Q.sentience_rights = 1; Q.rim_relation += 3; Q.outer_rc += 1; Q.midrim_rc += 1; Q.hawk_dissent += 2; SW.computeSupport(Q); }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if sentience_rights : The Senate proclaims that every sentient being in the Republic, human or not, holds the same rights under its laws. In the Core, some of the old families call it the end of civilisation. On the Rim, crowds gather to hear it read. ?][? if not sentience_rights : The declaration is voted down. In the Core, the human-first clubs celebrate. ?]

@patronage_1
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_rimaffairs = 1
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Outer Rim. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'rimaffairs', 'rc', 1); !}

Relief for the Rim goes out through sector governors who have pledged their support to the Caucus, and the contracts go to their cousins. Most of the grain arrives. The governors make sure everyone knows whom to thank.

@patronage_2
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_rimaffairs = 2
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Outer Rim. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'rimaffairs', 'rc', 2); !}

New hyperspace beacons, long promised to the Outer Rim, go up in sectors whose senators vote with us. The sectors next door, which did not, keep navigating by dead reckoning. Everyone draws the obvious lesson.

@patronage_3
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_rimaffairs = 3
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Mid Rim and the Expansion Region. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'rimaffairs', 'rc', 3); !}

The committee grants charters to settle a string of newly surveyed worlds in the Expansion Region, every one of them to a consortium with friends in the Caucus. The settlers will come later. The gratitude comes at once.

@patronage_4
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_rimaffairs = 4
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Outer Rim. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'rimaffairs', 'rc', 4); !}

In three disputed Outer Rim systems, each claimed by two rival governments, the committee recognises the claimants who have pledged their votes to the Caucus. The losers appeal to the Senate. The Senate is busy.

@patronage_5
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_rimaffairs = 5
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Core Worlds. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'rimaffairs', 'rc', 5); !}

Mining rights on a dozen Outer Rim worlds are sold, cheaply, to Core Worlds firms whose directors support the Caucus. The Core is pleased. The miners on those worlds were not consulted.

@patronage_6
view-if: not senators_expelled and pork_v_rimaffairs = 6
subtitle: +1 political capital, and support in the Mid Rim and the Expansion Region. Corruption rises and faith in the Republic falls.
on-arrival: {! SW.porkBarrel(Q, 'rimaffairs', 'rc', 6); !}

Grants to resettle refugees from the troubled Rim go to Mid Rim worlds whose senators vote with us, at a generous rate per head. The refugees get a roof, mostly. Their hosts get a windfall, and a reason to stay loyal.
